  "confirmed": [
    "Save bytes increase at every observed checkpoint in each case; this is persisted content, not only a transient managed-heap observation.",
    "Knowledge Activities/TimeUses/Mastery/Evidence are retained histories; Begin/Complete call SaveKnowledge, which typed-clones all saved knowledge lists. CanReserve and ReplaceActivity scan histories. No percentage attribution is measured.",
    "CollectedManagedBytes performs two forced full GCs then GC.GetTotalMemory over the whole shared process; four cases are sequential, not isolated processes. The current Checkpoint state clone is made after that memory sample.",
    "GameWorld holds canonical Knowledge plus its detached KnowledgeAuthority snapshot. GameSaveStore performs full Decode/Restore validation for existing/temporary/backup slots and Load. Those real IO/check costs are in case elapsed time.",
    "Retained managed bytes decrease at later checkpoints although save bytes and completed activities increase; actual values are in checkpoint_trends. This does not identify which cache or object graph remains live."
  ],
  "unconfirmed": [
    "Exact byte contributions of each authority ledger/history are not observable from uploaded slot metadata alone.",
    "Prior case/local snapshot JIT liveness and framework JSON/array-pool caches may contribute to spikes; no heap trace proves which one. No explicit application-wide GameWorld cache was found in the searched paths.",
    "Only aggregate checkpoint elapsed times exist; advance/validation/query/codec/IO allocation and CPU percentages cannot be separated without a later authorized profile."
  ],
  "interpretation": "Keep all original time/memory/save failures. Measurement-scope confounding is not a waiver or a reason to raise budgets."
